# open-delegate routing

Prefer cheaper OpenCode alternatives when delegating work out of the current Cursor chat.

## When to use `ode_delegate` (+ `ode_await`)

If a persona / Task request names a model that is:

1. in **ODE_MODELS** — the built-in cheap force catalog, or whatever `OPEN_DELEGATE_ODE_MODELS` / the live `ode_delegate` tool description lists, **or**
2. an OpenCode id starting with `openrouter/`,

you **must** call `ode_delegate` then `ode_await` (or `ode_status`), **not** the native Task / subagent tool.

Pass the OpenCode `provider/model` id as-is. Do not invent Cursor-slug remaps and do not “helpfully” upgrade to Anthropic/OpenAI flagships (Opus, Sonnet, Fable, GPT Sol/Terra).

## When to prefer native Task

Use the native Task / subagent tool only when the named model is **Cursor-native** and **not** on the ODE_MODELS force list.

## How to drive the bridge

Follow skill `ode-delegate` for the core loop (`ode_delegate` → `ode_await` → transcript / resume / cancel). Omit `model` to use `OPEN_DELEGATE_DEFAULT_MODEL` or the OpenCode server default (prefer a cheap Zen free pin when configuring).
